From: Eric Tanner <eric.tanner@harvia.com>
Subject: [PATCH] vt-sbc-am62l: dts: leave the AP6256 Wi-Fi/BT module unpowered

U-Boot carries its own copy of the board DT, and like the kernel's it
forced the Wi-Fi/BT module's load switch on from SPL: vcc_wifi was
regulator-always-on + regulator-boot-on, GPIO_WIFI_EN was muxed with a
pull-up, and sdhci2 was enabled so the SDIO host was bound (bootph-all)
with that regulator as its vmmc.

The product has no Wi-Fi or Bluetooth driver, so this only adds to the
current the board draws during boot - and on a long 5 V cable the boot
peak is what browns it out. Drop the flags, pull the enable down at the
pad, and disable the SDIO host. The kernel side is the matching
vt-sbc-am62l-leave-the-wifi-bt-module-unpowered.patch in
recipes-kernel/linux.

Signed-off-by: Eric Tanner <eric.tanner@harvia.com>
---
--- a/dts/upstream/src/arm64/ti/vt-sbc-am62l.dts
+++ b/dts/upstream/src/arm64/ti/vt-sbc-am62l.dts
@@ -90,8 +90,6 @@
 		regulator-min-microvolt = <3300000>;
 		regulator-max-microvolt = <3300000>;
 		enable-active-high;
-		regulator-always-on;
-		regulator-boot-on;
 		startup-delay-us = <200000>;
 		gpio = <&main_gpio0 55 GPIO_ACTIVE_HIGH>;
 		pinctrl-names = "default";
@@ -267,7 +265,7 @@
 	};
 	wifi_pwr_pins_default: wifi-pwr-default-pins {
 		pinctrl-single,pins = <
-			AM62PX_IOPAD(0x0120, PIN_OUTPUT_PULLUP, 7) /* (AC10) RGMII1_TD0 GPIO_WIFI_EN*/
+			AM62PX_IOPAD(0x0120, PIN_OUTPUT_PULLDOWN, 7) /* (AC10) RGMII1_TD0 GPIO_WIFI_EN*/
 		>;
 	};
 	main_mcan0_pins_default: main-mcan0-default-pins {
@@ -439,7 +437,7 @@
 	vmmc-supply = <&vcc_wifi>;
 	pinctrl-names = "default";
 	pinctrl-0 = <&main_mmc2_pins_default>;
-	status = "okay";
+	status = "disabled";
 	bootph-all;
 	no-sd;
 	no-mmc;
